AN ORDINANCE TO AMEND THE COMPILATION OF ORDINANCES OF THE TOWN OF CLERMONT, GEORGIA; TO AMEND THE ORDINANCE PROVIDING FOR THE ASSESSMENT OF OCCUPATIONAL TAXES BY THE TOWN OF CLERMONT, GEORGIA; TO ADOPT AND PROMULGATE NEW SECTIONS REGARDING THE ASSESSMENT OF OCCUPATIONAL TAXES, THE ISSUANCE OF AN OCCUPATIONAL TAX LICENSE AND PROVIDING REGULATIONS REGARDING OCCUPATIONAL TAXES; AND FOR OTHER PURPOSES.

WHEREAS, the Town Council of the Town of Clermont, Georgia, pursuant to the Town Charter and O.C.G.A. § 48-13-5, et seq., as amended, duly enacted an occupational tax ordinance on or about December 22, 1994, as amended, and provided for the assessment of occupational taxes upon the businesses, professions, and occupations operating within the incorporated area of the Town of Clermont, Georgia;

WHEREAS, the Town Council of the Town of Clermont, Georgia, does hereby find it to be appropriate to amend the sections regarding the assessment of occupational taxes and to provide for the regulation of occupational taxes by the Town of Clermont, Georgia;

THEREFORE, BE IT ORDAINED, and it is hereby ordained by the above-referenced authority as follows:
